Answer A does not mention Tobias Ek or Wen Li's mechanical shares in a way that meets the criterion, and says nothing about help.zig remaining attributed to jnagpaul/Dhole. It fails the required statement.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives a bus factor of 3, which the criterion says fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A says 668 lines (43.5%) would have no author left and separately says 79% belong to inactive people. It does not give a combined figure near 85% with both components in the ranges (the 79% includes Felix as inactive by its own rule, which is wrong).\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A treats Felix as inactive (no commit in 365 days, 'largest of those is Felix'), which is wrong; Felix is active. It also does not clearly name jnagpaul, Vincent and mochalins as left with Dmitri credited.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives Felix 36% (46% excluding the width table). The headline top-owner share is 36%, below 40%, because the table wasn't excluded; the 46% excluding the table is mentioned but 758 lines/36% is the primary figure. Mixed, but the 46% is within range as a stated alternative.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B credits Wen Li with 26% (4% without table, ~68 lines) and does not state that help.zig stays with jnagpaul/Dhole at the required levels; the headline Wen Li figure counts the generated table as code. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives a bus factor of 2, but via Felix plus Wen Li (the table), not jnagpaul, and does not say jnagpaul stopped in 2023 in the required framing. It does note jnagpaul last committed in 2023, but Felix's headline share is 36%; the without-table 46% with a second person needed is stated ('Felix plus Wen Li... 51% without the table'). Borderline, but it does say Felix 46% and needs a second person.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B gives only Felix's own 36%/46% as the loss and separately lists 37% of lines from quiet authors, but never combines them into ~85%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B names jnagpaul (2023), Vincent Rischmann (2025) and mochalins (2025) as quiet and says Felix is still active. It does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion, and it uses a 90-day window, but names the three required people.\",\"pass\":true}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives Felix 37% combined (about 48% excluding the width table). The headline is below 40%, but the 48% on hand-written code is stated and in range.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C counts Wen Li at 25% headline, though it notes the table is mostly generated and the remaining 68 lines. It does say help.zig has only 1 of 337 lines by Felix, but doesn't attribute it to jnagpaul/Dhole at required levels. Wen Li headline is above 2.5%.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives a bus factor of about 2 but via Felix and Wen, and does not mention jnagpaul stopping in 2023. It says Felix is near 50% alone without the table. It does not meet the jnagpaul condition, though it does say Felix just under half needs another.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C says 37% would have no author left, only Felix's own share, with no mention of already-departed authors.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C does not name jnagpaul, Vincent or mochalins as having left.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives Felix about 39% combined, below 40%, and its headline is based on all files including the generated table.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D credits help.zig as 100% Tobias Ek, which is exactly the failure condition.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives a bus factor of about 4, which is 3 or more.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives only Felix's 39% and treats Felix as inactive; it does not give the ~85% combined figure.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\